  ('social-190', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '노인 맞춤 돌봄·가사 간병 방문 지원이 속한 제도는?', null, '사회 서비스', array['공공 부조', '사회 보험', '적극적 평등 조치'], '{}'::text[], '사회 서비스는 도움이 필요한 모든 국민에게 상담·재활·돌봄 등 비금전적 지원을 원칙으로 제공한다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 4, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 189),
  ('social-191', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '수혜자 선정 과정에서 부정적 낙인이 생길 수 있는 제도 X. X의 재원은?', null, '조세(세금)', array['가입자 보험료', '수익자 부담', '기업 기부금'], '{}'::text[], '공공 부조는 국가·지자체가 조세로 전액 부담하며, 수혜자 선정 과정의 부정적 낙인과 재정 부담이 한계로 꼽힌다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 4, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 190),
  ('social-192', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '1차 사회 안전망 A, 2차 사회 안전망 B는?', null, '사회 보험–공공 부조', array['공공 부조–사회 보험', '사회 서비스–사회 보험', '공공 부조–사회 서비스'], '{}'::text[], '사회 보험이 1차 안전망으로 사회적 위험에 미리 대비하고, 그물에서 빠진 빈곤층을 공공 부조가 2차 안전망으로 받친다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 5, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 191),
  ('social-193', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '과거 자신의 노동과 관련 없이 급여가 보장되는 제도 X. X의 대상자는?', null, '생활이 어려운 빈곤층', array['일정 요건 갖춘 국민', '상시 근로자', '기여금을 낸 사람'], '{}'::text[], '공공 부조는 과거 노동·기여와 관계없이 생활이 어려운 빈곤층을 선별해 보장한다. 기여(보험료)와 연결되는 것은 사회 보험이다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 5, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 192),
  ('social-194', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '장애인 의무 고용 제도·여성 할당제가 속한 조치 X. X의 의의는?', null, '실질적 평등 실현', array['형식적 기회균등', '능력에 따른 우대', '시장 자율 경쟁'], '{}'::text[], '적극적 평등 실현 조치는 형식적 기회균등만으로 해결되지 않는 기울어진 운동장을 바로잡아 실질적 평등을 실현한다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 5, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 193),
  ('social-195', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '적극적 평등 실현 조치에 대한 설명으로 옳지 않은 것은?', null, '사회적 합의 불필요', array['역차별 논란 가능', '기울어진 운동장 교정', '직간접적 혜택 제공'], '{}'::text[], '적극적 평등 실현 조치는 역차별 논란이 생길 수 있어 시행할 때 사회적 합의가 필요하다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 5, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 194),
  ('social-196', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '공공 기관 지방 이전은 A, 지역 축제·고향 사랑 기부제는 B 정책이다. A–B는?', null, '과밀화 해소–자립형 발전', array['자립형 발전–과밀화 해소', '도시 내부 완화–과밀화 해소', '과밀화 해소–도시 내부 완화'], '{}'::text[], '「국가 균형 발전 특별법」의 공공 기관 지방 이전은 수도권 과밀화 해소, 지역 축제·고향 사랑 기부제는 자립형 지역 발전 기반 구축이다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 5, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 195),
  ('social-197', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '공공 임대 주택 공급·환경 정비 사업이 겨냥하는 불평등은?', null, '도시 내부 불평등', array['수도권 과밀화', '농촌 인구 고령화', '사회 계층 양극화'], '{}'::text[], '공공 임대 주택 공급, 도시 기반 시설 확충, 환경 정비 사업은 도시 내부 불평등 완화 정책이다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 5, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 196),
  ('social-198', 'social', 'choice', '불평등 완화 노력', null, '정의로운 사회를 위한 시민의 실천으로 옳지 않은 것은?', null, '정책은 정부에 일임', array['정책 제안 참여', '사회적 노력 감시·견제', '자신의 편견 성찰'], '{}'::text[], '시민은 정책을 다양한 방식으로 제안하고, 사회적 노력을 감시·견제하며, 자신의 선입견·편견을 성찰해야 한다.', '성신제T · 다양한 불평등 현상', 5, null, 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1etIcuZ7X0n_Y0iHDpN2ckiNnC9mlo0oH', 197),
  ('english-001', 'english', 'choice', 'Chichén Itzá', 'Made of stone, the city still stands.', '문장 앞에 생략된 접속사로 알맞은 것은?', 'Chichén Itzá was a major city of the Maya Empire from A.D. 750 to 1200. Made of stepped pyramids, temples, and other stone structures, the ancient city is now one of Mexico’s most visited tourist destinations. The largest building in Chichén Itzá is the Temple of Kukulkan ―a pyramid with 365 steps. A kind of calendar, the temple shows the change of seasons. On the spring and autumn equinoxes each year, a shadow falls on the pyramid in the shape of a snake. As the sun sets, this shadowy snake goes down the steps to eventually join a carved snake head on the pyramid’s side. The Mayans constructed the pyramids with carved stone. Amazingly, they worked without wheels or metal tools. To build a pyramid, Mayan workers created a base and added smaller and smaller levels as the structure rose. Building the pyramids required many workers. Some pyramids took hundreds of years to complete. Chichén Itzá was both an advanced city center and a religious site. Spanish records show that the Mayans made human sacrifices to a rain god here. Archaeologists have found bones, jewelry, and other objects that people wore when they were sacrificed. Experts also know that the Mayans were knowledgeable astronomers. They used the tops of the pyramids to view Venus and other planets.

[문제의 대상 문장·표현]
Made of stone, the city still stands.', 'Because', array['Although', 'Unless', 'Until'], '{}'::text[], 'Made of stone은 이유를 나타내는 분사구문이다. Because(As) it is made of stone에서 접속사·주어·be동사가 생략됐다.', '학습지1', 1, null, null, 0),
  ('english-002', 'english', 'choice', 'Chichén Itzá', 'Made of stepped pyramids, the city is famous.', 'Made of ~ 부분의 문법 이름은?', 'Chichén Itzá was a major city of the Maya Empire from A.D. 750 to 1200. Made of stepped pyramids, temples, and other stone structures, the ancient city is now one of Mexico’s most visited tourist destinations. The largest building in Chichén Itzá is the Temple of Kukulkan ―a pyramid with 365 steps. A kind of calendar, the temple shows the change of seasons. On the spring and autumn equinoxes each year, a shadow falls on the pyramid in the shape of a snake. As the sun sets, this shadowy snake goes down the steps to eventually join a carved snake head on the pyramid’s side. The Mayans constructed the pyramids with carved stone. Amazingly, they worked without wheels or metal tools. To build a pyramid, Mayan workers created a base and added smaller and smaller levels as the structure rose. Building the pyramids required many workers. Some pyramids took hundreds of years to complete. Chichén Itzá was both an advanced city center and a religious site. Spanish records show that the Mayans made human sacrifices to a rain god here. Archaeologists have found bones, jewelry, and other objects that people wore when they were sacrificed. Experts also know that the Mayans were knowledgeable astronomers. They used the tops of the pyramids to view Venus and other planets.

[문제의 대상 문장·표현]
Made of stepped pyramids, the city is famous.', '분사구문', array['동명사 주어', '명령문', '가정법 과거'], '{}'::text[], '과거분사 Made로 시작해 주절을 꾸미는 분사구문이다. "계단식 피라미드로 이루어져 있어서"라는 이유를 나타낸다.', '학습지1', 1, null, null, 1),
  ('english-003', 'english', 'choice', 'Chichén Itzá', 'the Temple of Kukulkan', 'Kukulkan은 어떤 존재일까?', 'Chichén Itzá was a major city of the Maya Empire from A.D. 750 to 1200. Made of stepped pyramids, temples, and other stone structures, the ancient city is now one of Mexico’s most visited tourist destinations. The largest building in Chichén Itzá is the Temple of Kukulkan ―a pyramid with 365 steps. A kind of calendar, the temple shows the change of seasons. On the spring and autumn equinoxes each year, a shadow falls on the pyramid in the shape of a snake. As the sun sets, this shadowy snake goes down the steps to eventually join a carved snake head on the pyramid’s side. The Mayans constructed the pyramids with carved stone. Amazingly, they worked without wheels or metal tools. To build a pyramid, Mayan workers created a base and added smaller and smaller levels as the structure rose. Building the pyramids required many workers. Some pyramids took hundreds of years to complete. Chichén Itzá was both an advanced city center and a religious site. Spanish records show that the Mayans made human sacrifices to a rain god here. Archaeologists have found bones, jewelry, and other objects that people wore when they were sacrificed. Experts also know that the Mayans were knowledgeable astronomers. They used the tops of the pyramids to view Venus and other planets.

[문제의 대상 문장·표현]
the Temple of Kukulkan', '뱀 모양의 신', array['비를 내리는 왕', '마야의 달력', '태양 관측탑'], '{}'::text[], 'Kukulkan은 마야의 뱀신이다. 그래서 춘분·추분에 뱀 모양 그림자가 계단을 내려오는 신전이 그의 이름을 갖는다.', '학습지1', 1, null, null, 2),
  ('english-004', 'english', 'choice', 'Chichén Itzá', 'the spring and autumn equinoxes', '이 표현의 뜻은?', 'Chichén Itzá was a major city of the Maya Empire from A.D. 750 to 1200. Made of stepped pyramids, temples, and other stone structures, the ancient city is now one of Mexico’s most visited tourist destinations. The largest building in Chichén Itzá is the Temple of Kukulkan ―a pyramid with 365 steps. A kind of calendar, the temple shows the change of seasons. On the spring and autumn equinoxes each year, a shadow falls on the pyramid in the shape of a snake. As the sun sets, this shadowy snake goes down the steps to eventually join a carved snake head on the pyramid’s side. The Mayans constructed the pyramids with carved stone. Amazingly, they worked without wheels or metal tools. To build a pyramid, Mayan workers created a base and added smaller and smaller levels as the structure rose. Building the pyramids required many workers. Some pyramids took hundreds of years to complete. Chichén Itzá was both an advanced city center and a religious site. Spanish records show that the Mayans made human sacrifices to a rain god here. Archaeologists have found bones, jewelry, and other objects that people wore when they were sacrificed. Experts also know that the Mayans were knowledgeable astronomers. They used the tops of the pyramids to view Venus and other planets.

