[연습용 문장·표현]
‘나는 그에게 우체국에 가 달라고 부탁했다.’를 ask로 영작하고, ‘He would spend hours staring at the wall.’의 would와 바꿔 쓸 수 있는 표현을 쓰시오.', 'I asked him to go to the post office. / used to (He used to spend hours staring at the wall.)', '{}'::text[], array['asked + him + to go', 'to the post office', 'would = used to (과거의 습관)'], '', '학습지3', 1, null, null, 1011),
  ('english-written-013', 'english', 'written', '가정법', null, '‘내가 부자라면 그 집을 살 수 있을 텐데.’(지금 부자가 아님)를 가정법 과거로 쓰고, If를 생략한 문장도 쓰시오.', '[연습용 문장·표현]
‘내가 부자라면 그 집을 살 수 있을 텐데.’(지금 부자가 아님)를 가정법 과거로 쓰고, If를 생략한 문장도 쓰시오.', 'If I were rich, I could buy the house. / Were I rich, I could buy the house.', '{}'::text[], array['If + I + were (be동사는 were)', 'could + 동사원형 buy', 'If 생략 시 Were I rich 도치'], '', '학습지3', 4, null, null, 1012),
  ('english-written-014', 'english', 'written', '가정법', null, '‘그는 마치 모든 것을 아는 것처럼 말한다.’와 ‘그녀는 마치 그 사고를 직접 본 것처럼 말한다.’를 as if로 영작하시오.', '[연습용 문장·표현]
‘그는 마치 모든 것을 아는 것처럼 말한다.’와 ‘그녀는 마치 그 사고를 직접 본 것처럼 말한다.’를 as if로 영작하시오.', 'He talks as if he knew everything. / She speaks as if she had seen the accident with her own eyes.', '{}'::text[], array['as if + 과거형 knew (현재의 반대)', 'as if + had seen (이전 일의 반대)', '두 문장 주절 현재시제'], '', '학습지3', 4, null, null, 1013),
  ('english-written-015', 'english', 'written', '측정의 일관성', null, '‘Following this logic, units need reliable definitions.’를 If로 시작하는 부사절 문장으로 바꾸고, 이 문장의 동사가 과거형으로 바뀌지 않는 이유를 쓰시오.', 'To harness the full potential of units of measurement, we need some degree of consistency. Subjective measures contain useful knowledge, but this can be difficult to share, based as it is on an individual’s experience. The historian of science Theodore M. Porter describes measurement as a ʻtechnology of distance’: a tool that uses shared rules to bridge differences of culture and geography, allowing for the exchange of information. Following this logic, if measurement is another sort of language, then just as with words, individual units need reliable definitions in order to communicate. In the earliest societies, these definitions might need to be shared no more widely than a single settlement, meaning that the definition can be no more complex than knowing that a unit was equal to a certain body part. As these communities grew in size, though, the inadequacies of this system would become evident. Imagine a disagreement over trade or tribute: it is a moment of conflict that demands greater consistency in measurement.

[문제의 대상 문장·표현]
‘Following this logic, units need reliable definitions.’를 If로 시작하는 부사절 문장으로 바꾸고, 이 문장의 동사가 과거형으로 바뀌지 않는 이유를 쓰시오.', 'If we follow this logic, units need reliable definitions. 실제로 가능한 조건을 말하는 직설법 조건문이라서 가정법처럼 시제를 과거로 바꾸지 않는다.', '{}'::text[], array['If we follow this logic', '주절 현재시제 유지', '가정법이 아닌 직설법 조건이라는 설명'], '', '학습지4', 2, null, null, 1014),
  ('english-written-016', 'english', 'written', '측정의 일관성', null, '‘It is difficult to share, based as it is on an individual’s experience.’에서 based as it is on을 as로 시작하는 절로 바꾸고, 문장 전체를 우리말로 해석하시오.', 'To harness the full potential of units of measurement, we need some degree of consistency. Subjective measures contain useful knowledge, but this can be difficult to share, based as it is on an individual’s experience. The historian of science Theodore M. Porter describes measurement as a ʻtechnology of distance’: a tool that uses shared rules to bridge differences of culture and geography, allowing for the exchange of information. Following this logic, if measurement is another sort of language, then just as with words, individual units need reliable definitions in order to communicate. In the earliest societies, these definitions might need to be shared no more widely than a single settlement, meaning that the definition can be no more complex than knowing that a unit was equal to a certain body part. As these communities grew in size, though, the inadequacies of this system would become evident. Imagine a disagreement over trade or tribute: it is a moment of conflict that demands greater consistency in measurement.

[문제의 대상 문장·표현]
‘It is difficult to share, based as it is on an individual’s experience.’에서 based as it is on을 as로 시작하는 절로 바꾸고, 문장 전체를 우리말로 해석하시오.', 'as it is based on an individual’s experience / 그것은 개인의 경험에 기반하기 때문에 공유하기 어렵다.', '{}'::text[], array['as it is based on', 'as = ~이기 때문에 (이유)', '개인의 경험·공유하기 어렵다 해석'], '', '학습지4', 2, null, null, 1015),
